    "result_text": "All 268 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` integer field to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` (with `getMembershipNumber`/`setMembershipNumber`) at build time, so the mapper picks it up automatically by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient Integer membershipNumber` field with getter/setter. It's transient because the number is derived at creation time and returned in the response, not a persisted column.\n\n3. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new function) \u2014 Computes `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` and sets it on the owner.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `assignMembershipNumber` step into the create pipeline (after the duplicate checks, before `save`), under the same transaction governance. Because the count is taken before the new owner is saved, it correctly equals \"one more than the current number of owners\".\n\n5. **Test** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to compute the expected number from the repository and assert `$.membershipNumber` on the response.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps `membershipNumber` from `Owner` to `OwnerDto` by name, so `RespondWithOwnerCreated` returns it with no mapper change needed. The number is only populated on the create path (transient), so GET/list responses simply omit it \u2014 consistent with the spec, which only requires assigning it to newly created owners.",
